    add('Objective','Learn set-specific relationships with one set-generic algorithm: card-to-shell/factor, card-to-card, pool-to-factor and candidate compatibility with the existing pool. Q is intrinsic strength, L availability, A relationship/strategy fit, D projected-deck improvement. No authored set/color archetype rules or neural network. Structure is fitted without wins; game outcomes and target modal builds are joined only for labeled evaluation/descriptions.\n\nThe preregistration was committed as `bbf2693` before performance analysis. A scale clarification, `a47bac2`, prospectively fixed representation comparison to a shared binary inclusion target rather than incomparable MAEs on binary/count scales. Calibration DMU/BRO/WOE fits representation, context and family parameters; development LCI/MKM/OTJ/ONE/MOM selects the family and tests the gate. [Plan](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/preregistration.json).')
    add('Production A audit','Current A is an empirical pair-GIH lift conditional on an active authored set/pair profile. Activation requires confidence>=.35 and lead>=.10. Pair GIH is shrunk toward overall GIH with prior300, compared against pair/overall baselines, normalized by .04 and converted to `.5+.5*affinity*activeConfidence`. Missing/unsettled pair evidence gives neutral A. Production retains this contract.\n\nHistorical replay snapshots have no qualified pair-GIH table, so current A is predominantly neutral; this is a missing-input baseline, not proof that production archetype evidence is ineffective. The experimental study learns composition relationships, not another GIH bonus. [Existing implementation](src/DraftTG.RecommendationEngine/ArchetypeRecommendationEngine.cs).')
    add('Build corpus qualification',f'{qual["qualifiedAll"]:,} conservative builds across {len(qual["datasets"])} existing datasets; {qual["modelQualified"]:,} in eight modeled Premier sets. Of these, **{fitCount:,} fit / {auditCount:,} internal evidence-audit / {targetCount:,} target builds**. Original approximately85k Phase B primary builds include spent sets and less reliable configurations; they are not all model training rows.\n\n'+table(['Set','Primary available','Qualified','Fit','Audit','Target'],[(a['set'],a['counts']['availablePrimaryBuilds'],a['counts'].get('qualified',0),a['partitions'].get('fit',0),a['partitions'].get('audit',0),a['partitions'].get('target',0)) for a in qual['datasets']])+'\n\nRequire resolved positive integer counts, exactly40 cards, unique source mode, >=3 observed games, one observed configuration and12–20 lands. Multiple configurations decline because saved summaries retain total games but **not exact mode support**. Single-configuration support equals observed game count. HIGH means>=5 games and opening/modal agreement; MEDIUM covers other eligible builds; LOW declines. Data are reused from attributed 17Lands public bulk sources and the pinned TrevorJS transformation, plus the owned Scryfall identity catalog; source hashes and bounded-prefix caveats remain in the [Phase B source audit](docs/evidence/v2-phase-b/source-audit.json). No new acquisition/provider request occurred. Existing aggregate ties, non40 configurations, opening agreement, main colors, land counts and mode-support distributions remain in [qualification](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/build-qualification.json). Missing opening agreement is not proven disagreement. Bounded histories are not proven complete; **zero final submitted decks are asserted**.')
    add('Build representation',f'Compared binary presence, normalized copies, nonland normalized copies, and square-root counts capped at3. Selected **{rep["selected"]["representation"]}**, calibration common-target inclusion MAE {n(rep["selected"]["macroMAE"])}. Basics are excluded; nonbasic lands remain in the selected card vector while land/fixing summaries are separate. Pool inference excludes lands. The nonland-only alternative was tested, not silently assumed.\n\n'+table(['Representation','Context','Calibration inclusion MAE'],[(r['representation'],r['context'],n(r['macroMAE'])) for r in rep['results']])+'\n\nStructured creature/noncreature counts, curve0–6+, early plays, mana value, land counts, splash spell loads, assigned removal and fixing are descriptive. Untagged removal/synergy roles remain **unknown**, not zero; assigned coverage is a lower bound. No role bonus enters model fitting. [Feature coverage](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/build-features.json).')
    add('Color-shell analysis','Compared two strongest nonland spell-color loads, broad >=15% spell-color support, and a global model. **Two-color shell wins calibration reconstruction.** Gold spell loads split by colors; basics do not determine the shell. Lesser spell colors are recorded as splashes. Shell labels are learned context keys, not labels such as UR=spells.\n\nAt inference the pool gets soft beliefs over supported shells; the candidate cannot alter this prior. Color identity alone is controlled by same-color distractors and a tied color-only baseline. Within-shell factors permit multiple strategies in one pair. Fixing lands/splash artifacts do not automatically redefine the base shell.')
    add('Frequency baselines','Color-only assigns tied scores within matched colors. Shell frequency predicts inclusion conditional on pool-inferred shell; Q-only uses frozen current-k500 raw Q. Frequency-plus-Q ranks `log(inclusion)+2*Q`. All evaluated candidates/control cards are identical per task. Pair base expectation additionally controls within-shell factor prevalence and marginal inclusion.\n\nThe main completion controls use the calibration-selected A-family pool weighting (quality). The frozen cold/full run also exports a **uniform-pool frequency control** on the same tasks. This stronger comparator is reported separately below; it does not rescue qualification. Successful-build uplift is descriptive only, never part of these scoring controls. No prevalence/frequency difference is claimed to be causal synergy.')
    add('Candidate A/B/C methodology','**A:** regularized shell inclusion profiles, no explicit latent archetypes. **B:** A plus soft within-shell factor inclusion residual. **C:** B plus regularized pair residual to the existing pool. All families share one generic implementation; the learned cards differ by set.\n\n'+table(['Family','Calibration pool weight','Evidence prior','Calibration matched MRR'],[(f,fit0['selected'][f]['weight'],fit0['selected'][f]['cold'],n(fit0['selected'][f]['MRR'])) for f in ('A','B','C')])+'\n\nAll selected evidence-prior50; A uses frozen-Q-weighted pool membership, B/C uniform. Representation/contexts fit first, then family parameters on disjoint calibration evidence-audit completion; development selects C. Cold priors50/250/500 are confidence budgets, not measured posterior certainty. No post-development parameter changes.')
    add('Archetype discovery','Deterministic nonnegative matrix factorization, ranks1/2/4, 100 multiplicative updates, no outcome inputs. Fit vocabulary includes all nonbasic cards for marginals; factor vocabulary requires>=20 fit builds. A separate internal fit/audit split chooses the smallest rank with>=1% reconstruction gain over rank1, matched-factor cosine>=.8 across a hash-independent half-sample, and every factor>=25 effective builds. Otherwise retain rank1.\n\n'+table(['Set','Shells','Total factors','Factors per shell'],[(s['set'],len(s['diagnostics']),sum(d['factors'] for d in s['diagnostics']),f'{min(d["factors"] for d in s["diagnostics"])}–{max(d["factors"] for d in s["diagnostics"])}') for s in fit0['diagnostics']])+'\n\nExact shell-to-factor counts are also in the machine-readable summary and full fit evidence. Factors are automatically numbered; no name is required for scoring. Top loading-to-shell ratios, prevalence, curve and creature traits are published in [descriptions](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/archetype-diagnostics.json). These are stable statistical deck families, not proof of human archetype names.')
    add('Cluster/factor stability','Soft memberships sum to1 and support mixed themes. NMF factors are matched across resamples by maximum permutation-averaged cosine; factor numbering alone has no meaning. The .8 threshold guards retained multi-factor models. Complete rank1/2/4 reconstruction, support and resample tables are in [fit evidence](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/model-fit.json).\n\nNested learning curves separately compare fitted inclusion loadings with the full model. Different-rank comparisons are unavailable rather than assigned a synthetic stability score. Half-sample stability is a heuristic, not a bootstrap confidence interval; full factor stability does not guarantee causal synergy.')
    add('Card-card affinity',f'{pairs["pairs"]:,} retained residual relationships: {pairs["positive"]:,} positive / {pairs["negative"]:,} negative. For each: source set/format/shell, observed count, latent expected count, effect, confidence and source-model SHA256 are preserved. Maximum absolute regularized effect {n(pairs["maximumAbsoluteEffect"])}. Full pairs remain ignored; portable top examples and complete-artifact hash are in [pair evidence](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/pair-affinity.json).\n\nExpected co-occurrence is the sum of per-build latent inclusion products. Effect is `clip(log((observed+5)/(expected+5)),-1,1)*expected/(expected+50)`. Require expected>=5 and both marginals>=20; positive observed>=5. Low-observed negative relationships additionally require expected>=20 and marginals>=30. A2/2 coincidence returns exactly zero. Confidence is regularization strength, not a calibrated probability of synergy.')
    add('Frequency/power controls','The primary task matches exact colors, mana value within1, raw Q within.10 and fit frequency ratio between.5 and2. All four distractors are absent from the target build. This prevents simple off-color/bomb-vs-poor-card tests, but coarse Q and frequency matches cannot remove all observational selection bias.\n\nPair expectations condition on latent shell composition; marginal power/frequency is not counted as an independent synergy vote. Low-frequency cards cannot create factors, and regularized pair effects are bounded. The primary matched-task gain is modest and fails the gate; no statistical significance or causal Limited-win benefit is asserted.')
    add('Pool-to-archetype inference','Only `PoolBeforePick`, candidate identity, disjoint models and optionally frozen Q weighting enter inference. Pool shell belief uses prevalence plus weighted log inclusion ratios, softmaxed; factor belief uses prevalence plus weighted factor-to-shell inclusion ratios. Candidate cards are scored against this fixed belief; they never teach it.\n\nPool multiplicity uses the selected sqrt cap3 transform. The compatibility value combines shell-relative inclusion, latent residual and (C only) weighted average pair residual to existing nonland pool cards. No target final build, future picks/offers, win record, R/commitment or optimizer result enters inference. P1P1 is exact fallback; a one-card pool has at most1/9 pool-confidence budget, so early belief grows smoothly. [Prediction provenance](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/prediction-provenance.json).')
    add('Experimental A formula','Let `g_i` be global regularized inclusion, `p_si` shell inclusion, `p_ki` factor inclusion, `w_s` pool shell belief and `u_sk` pool factor belief.\n\n```text\nA raw = sum_s w_s * log(p_si/g_i)\nB raw = A raw + sum_s w_s * log(sum_k u_sk*p_ki / p_si)\nC raw = B raw + sum_s w_s * weighted_mean_pool(pairResidual_s(i,j))\nfit = .5 + .25*tanh(raw)\nconfidence = poolSupport/(poolSupport+8) * sum_s w_s*n_s/(n_s+50)\nexperimental A = current A + confidence*(fit-current A)\n```\n\nShell/factor log beliefs divide the weighted log-evidence sum by4 and include prevalence priors. Inclusion shrinkage uses50 builds toward set/shell marginals. Fit lies [.25,.75], confidence[0,1]. Missing model/card, unsupported shell, land candidate or empty pool retains original A. Offline recomposition uses the actual frozen calibration and weights; Q/L/D/R/commitment, priors and deck projections are copied. No production configuration installs this formula.')
    add('Build-completion metrics','Mask all copies of one hash-selected nonland card from a disjoint target modal build, then rank it against four distractors. At most one task per target draft and500/set; all sets reach500. Full remaining build is the completion pool; this is **not a historical pick-time task**. Tied rankings get expected reciprocal rank and fractional TopK credit.\n\n'+table(['Partition/model','Top1','Top3','MRR','Normalized rank'],[(part+'/'+f,pc(metric[f]['Top1']),pc(metric[f]['Top3']),n(metric[f]['MRR']),n(metric[f]['normalizedRank'])) for part,metric in (('calibration target',cal),('development',dev)) for f in ('A','B','C','frequency','Q','color-only')])+'\n\nThese calibration-target results are separate from internal evidence-audit numbers used to fit parameters. Same-color relaxed completion is secondary and cannot pass the gate. [Completion evidence](docs/evidence/v2-phase-d/build-completion.json).')
